1
00:00:00,591 --> 00:00:04,051
(Leonard:)...which they threw intentionally
incomplete to avoid loss of yardage...

2
00:00:04,219 --> 00:00:05,969
(Leonard:)...or to conserve time.

3
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:09,930
I can't believe they're not penalized
with the loss of a down...

4
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:14,350
(Leonard:)...and by having to move the line of
scrimmage back to the spot of the foul.

5
00:00:17,191 --> 00:00:20,781
(Penny:)-Here. Have some pizza, sweetie.
-Penny, you know I'm lactose intolerant.

6
00:00:20,945 --> 00:00:23,075
(Penny:)I know.
I just need you to stop talking.

7
00:00:25,032 --> 00:00:28,372
Penny. Penny. Penny.

8
00:00:29,703 --> 00:00:31,793
(Penny:)-Sheldon, come in.
-Thank you.

9
00:00:31,956 --> 00:00:35,246
(Sheldon:)I'd like to make a sandwich,
but I'm out of bread.

10
00:00:36,543 --> 00:00:40,173
(Penny:)-There's some in the fridge.
-You shouldn't keep bread in the fridge.

11
00:00:40,339 --> 00:00:43,129
(Sheldon:)Staleness is caused
by crystallization of the starch...

12
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:45,430
(Sheldon:)...which occurs faster
at cool temperatures.

13
00:00:45,594 --> 00:00:48,304
On Earth, we say, "Thank you."

14
00:00:49,181 --> 00:00:52,181
(Sheldon:)So, Leonard, how goes the mimesis?

15
00:00:52,351 --> 00:00:57,061
(Sheldon:)-Mimesis?
-You know, mimesis.

16
00:00:57,231 --> 00:01:00,021
(Sheldon:)An action in which the mimic
takes on the properties...

